# Plan (opus, strong)

**Goal.** All five background loops `app::serve` spawns (the matchmaker, the series sweeper, the reaper, the retention purge, the bot pool) start through a new supervisor, `jackioh_server::loops::spawn_supervised`. When a panic unwinds out of a loop, the supervisor logs `loop.crashed` (an alert) with the loop's name and the panic message, waits `LOOP_RESTART_DELAY_SECONDS`, logs `loop.restarted` and starts the loop again. The loops' own per-tick `Result` handling stays exactly as it is: none of the five `run_*` functions changes. A test shows that a loop which panics in one tick is logged under its name and ticks again later, and that a loop which returns is not restarted.

